<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Minimal static Psalm config, baked into the toolbox image at
  /opt/config/psalm.xml (see Dockerfile) and passed explicitly via psalm's
  config flag in run-sast-php.sh.

  2026-09-08: psalm hard-requires a config file in the analyzed project and
  refuses to run without one at all ("Could not locate a config XML file in
  path /workspace. Have you run 'psalm init' ?" — confirmed live against a
  real run). Since /workspace is bind-mounted read-only in this pipeline,
  running psalm's own init step could never write a config there even as a
  first pass. This file lives inside the image instead, and its
  directory name entry below is an absolute path, so it works regardless of
  psalm's own working directory or root-flag resolution.

  Schema confirmed against Psalm's own documented minimal example (a bare
  psalm/projectFiles element is valid with no namespace declaration
  required) — not guessed.

  errorLevel is set to 5 as a reasonable middle ground, not a carefully
  tuned value — this step is already documented (S6-1, sast-php's own Note
  in the orchestrator) as a SECONDARY PHP pass, with sast-multi-semgrep-php
  as the primary signal, so psalm's exact strictness here matters less than
  it existing at all. Adjust freely if psalm's findings prove too noisy or
  too quiet once real output exists to judge that from.
-->
<psalm errorLevel="5">
    <projectFiles>
        <directory name="/workspace" />
    </projectFiles>
</psalm>
